time="2025-08-31 21:40:37.282" level=debug msg="Processing stream completion" complete_response="Certainly! Below is a Python function that takes a string as input and returns its reversed version.\n\n```python\ndef reverse_string(s):\n    return s[::-1]\n\n# Example usage:\noriginal_string = \"Hello, World!\"\nreversed_string = reverse_string(original_string)\nprint(reversed_string)  # Output: \"!dlroW ,olleH\"\n```\n\n### Explanation:\n- `s[::-1]` is a slice operation that starts from the end of the string and moves backwards. This effectively reverses the string.\n\nYou can use this function to reverse any string you pass to it." conversation_id=7fe3fb04-c12e-45a0-90c4-3745260c2e06 tool_calls_count=0
time="2025-08-31 21:40:37.282" level=debug msg="handleLLMResponseComplete called" conversation_id=7fe3fb04-c12e-45a0-90c4-3745260c2e06 response="Certainly! Below is a Python function that takes a string as input and returns its reversed version.\n\n```python\ndef reverse_string(s):\n    return s[::-1]\n\n# Example usage:\noriginal_string = \"Hello, World!\"\nreversed_string = reverse_string(original_string)\nprint(reversed_string)  # Output: \"!dlroW ,olleH\"\n```\n\n### Explanation:\n- `s[::-1]` is a slice operation that starts from the end of the string and moves backwards. This effectively reverses the string.\n\nYou can use this function to reverse any string you pass to it." tool_calls_count=0
